                    {
                        "id": "21",
                        "text": "Paragraph 2: Explanation of the design of the experiment"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "22",
                        "text": "Explains the set-up of the experiment. Information on the materials used, how they were prepared for the study, and the duration of the experiment is included here."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "23",
                            "text": " Not less than 3 days after trapping, birds were trained to feed from "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "24",
                            "text": " an artificial flower containing 14% sucrose "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "25",
                            "text": " during the course of a day (6–9 h) "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "23",
                            "text": "."
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "26",
                            "text": " The “flower” was a red cardboard disk (diameter 4.5 cm) with a syringe cap inserted through its center to act as a well. The flower was taped with red tape to the top of a cane (1 m), which was pushed into the ground within 5 m of the usual position of the feeder. "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "23",
                            "text": " Observers sat at least 10 m from the flower. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Paragraph 2 here.",
                "id": "23"
            }
