            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "34",
                        "text": "Paragraph 3: Description of the experiment"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "35",
                        "text": "Describes the list of procedures followed in carrying out the experiment."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "36",
                            "text": " Following training, there were 2 experimental days: Treatment 1 and Treatment 2, which weather permitting immediately followed the training day. As on the training day, the feeder "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "37",
                            "text": " was removed and replaced "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "36",
                            "text": " with the artificial flower. In Treatment 1 "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "38",
                            "text": " (low, high, and low) "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "36",
                            "text": " , the flower contained 14% sucrose for the first 3 h, 25% sucrose for the next 3 h, and 14% sucrose for the final 3 h. In Treatment 2 "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "39",
                            "text": " (high, low, and high) "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "36",
                            "text": " , the flower contained 25% sucrose for the first 3 h, 14% sucrose for the next 3 h, and 25% sucrose for the final 3 h. Half the birds received Treatment 1 first and the other half Treatment 2 first. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Paragraph 3 here.",
                "id": "36"
            }
        },
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "41",
                        "text": "Paragraph 4: Explanation of the method"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "42",
                        "text": "Explains how the results were calculated. This includes information on how the calculations were obtained."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "43",
                            "text": " The volume drunk and the timing and duration of each of a bird's visit[s] to the flower were recorded during both training and treatment days. "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "44",
                            "text": " Volumes were measured by refilling the syringe cap using a repeating pipette accurate to 10 μl. Duration of a feeding bout was the interval between the first insertion of the bird's bill into the flower and the last withdrawal from the flower before flying away. "
                        }
                    ],
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "43",
                            "text": " (Bacon et al., 2011) For the full reference, see "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "43",
                            "text": "<a href=\"/references\">References</a>"
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "43",
                            "text": "."
                        }
                    ]
                ],
